{
  "name": "ST-Accounting / n8n Egress IP Auto-Heal",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "sched",
      "name": "Every 6h",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.ipify.org?format=json",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      },
      "id": "egress",
      "name": "Get Egress IP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        224,
        304
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/zones/f37c511cbdace29d635a401391029810/firewall/access_rules/rules/0d1f8030d83a451e88864eb7041219df",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      },
      "id": "getrule",
      "name": "Get CF Rule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        448,
        304
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "PeOPQC7Vhly9UzqD",
          "name": "Cloudflare Expense Tunnel token"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// ST-Accounting / n8n Egress IP Auto-Heal — v1.0\n// Compare current n8n egress IP to the IP in the Cloudflare IP Access rule.\n// Input: items[0]=ipify {ip}, items[1]=CF rule GET {result:{configuration:{value}}}\n// Output: { changed, newIp, oldIp, zone, ruleId }\nconst ipifyItem = $('Get Egress IP').first().json;\nconst cfItem = $('Get CF Rule').first().json;\nconst newIp = String(ipifyItem.ip || '').trim();\nconst oldIp = String(((cfItem.result||{}).configuration||{}).value || '').trim();\nif (!/^\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{1,3}){3}$/.test(newIp)) { throw new Error('ipify returned non-IP: '+newIp); }\nreturn [{ json: { changed: newIp !== oldIp && oldIp !== '', newIp, oldIp,\n  zone: 'f37c511cbdace29d635a401391029810', ruleId: '0d1f8030d83a451e88864eb7041219df' } }];\n"
      },
      "id": "cmp",
      "name": "Compare",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        672,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.changed }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "if",
      "name": "IP changed?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        880,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "url": "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/zones/f37c511cbdace29d635a401391029810/firewall/access_rules/rules/0d1f8030d83a451e88864eb7041219df",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ mode:'whitelist', configuration:{ target:'ip', value:$json.newIp }, notes:'n8n Render egress (auto-healed) — receipts ingest; bypass Bot Fight Mode' }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      },
      "id": "patch",
      "name": "Update CF Rule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1104,
        208
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "PeOPQC7Vhly9UzqD",
          "name": "Cloudflare Expense Tunnel token"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "sparkst@gmail.com",
        "subject": "=n8n egress IP changed → CF rule auto-updated ({{ $json.oldIp }} → {{ $json.newIp }})",
        "message": "=The n8n Render egress IP changed from {{ $json.oldIp }} to {{ $json.newIp }}.\\nThe Cloudflare IP Access rule was updated automatically so receipt uploads keep working.\\n\\nZone: {{ $json.zone }}\\nRule: {{ $json.ruleId }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "notify",
      "name": "Notify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1328,
        208
      ],
      "webhookId": "85b0cc4d-7811-421c-aec4-22b666428633",
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "UkRZygJdoRQl7US1",
          "name": "Sparkry Gmail"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## n8n Egress IP Auto-Heal\n\nKeeps the Cloudflare IP Access rule for books.sparkry.ai in sync with n8n's Render egress IP, so receipt uploads never break if Render rotates the IP.\n\n**Flow:** every 6h → get n8n's egress IP (ipify) → read the CF rule → if different, PATCH the rule + email you.\n\n### One-time setup\nBoth CF HTTP nodes use an **HTTP Header Auth** credential. Create it once:\n- Credential type: *Header Auth*\n- Name: `Authorization`\n- Value: `Bearer <CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN>` (the token with Zone:Firewall Services:Edit for sparkry.ai)\nThen select it on both **Get CF Rule** and **Update CF Rule**.\n\nGmail notify uses the existing **Sparkry Gmail** cred.\n\nZone `f37c511c…`, rule `0d1f8030…` are embedded (non-secret).",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "note",
      "name": "How it works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -464,
        160
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every 6h": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Get Egress IP",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Get Egress IP": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Get CF Rule",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Get CF Rule": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Compare",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Compare": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "IP changed?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "IP changed?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Update CF Rule",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        []
      ]
    },
    "Update CF Rule": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Notify",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "timezone": "America/Los_Angeles",
    "callerPolicy": "workflowsFromSameOwner",
    "executionTimeout": 300,
    "errorWorkflow": "iQi6zyArMZn0TzAT",
    "availableInMCP": false
  }
}
